  <div class="spec">Edexcel GCSE RS (1RB0) · Religion &amp; Ethics through Christianity</div>
  <div class="stage" id="stage">

    <!-- 0 WELCOME -->
    <section class="screen active" data-teach="intro">
      <span class="tag">Mini-Lesson</span>
      <h1>Christianity: Religion &amp; Ethics</h1>
      <p class="big">This mini-lesson works through the Edexcel GCSE Spec B topic <b>Religion and Ethics through a study of Christianity</b>: <b>Christian beliefs</b> about God, <b>marriage and the family</b>, <b>matters of life and death</b>, and the key <b>ethical reasoning</b> Christians use to make moral decisions.</p>
      <figure>
        <svg viewBox="0 0 560 150" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" role="img" aria-label="Christian beliefs shape Christian ethical decisions">
          <rect x="18" y="45" width="150" height="62" rx="14" fill="#d9ebff" stroke="#2c2840" stroke-width="3"/>
          <text x="93" y="72" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Fredoka" font-size="14" font-weight="600" fill="#0b5bbf">Christian</text>
          <text x="93" y="92" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Fredoka" font-size="13" fill="#0b5bbf">beliefs</text>
          <rect x="392" y="45" width="150" height="62" rx="14" fill="#ffe9c7" stroke="#2c2840" stroke-width="3"/>
          <text x="467" y="72" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Fredoka" font-size="14" font-weight="600" fill="#9a5a00">moral choices /</text>
          <text x="467" y="92" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Fredoka" font-size="13" fill="#9a5a00">how to live</text>
          <line x1="168" y1="76" x2="382" y2="76" stroke="#34c777" stroke-width="5"/>
          <polygon points="382,76 366,68 366,84" fill="#34c777"/>
          <text x="275" y="62" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Fredoka" font-size="13" font-weight="600" fill="#137a45">shape</text>
          <text x="275" y="100" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Nunito" font-size="12.5" fill="#6b6580">ethics flow from what Christians believe</text>
        </svg>
      </figure>
      <p>Work through each screen, answer the <b>questions</b> as you go (matching, definitions and short explanations) and collect ⭐ stars. Christian beliefs are stated as the tradition teaches them, and real differences (e.g. Catholic and liberal Protestant views) are noted. Press <b>Start</b> when you're ready.</p>
    </section>

    <!-- 1 WHAT THE TOPIC ASKS -->
    <section class="screen" data-teach="ultimate-reality">
      <span class="tag lo">The big question</span>
      <h2>What does this topic cover?</h2>
      <p>Edexcel Spec B Area of Study 1 studies <b>Religion and Ethics through Christianity</b>. It asks: what do Christians <b>believe</b>, and how do those beliefs guide their <b>moral choices</b>?</p>
      <ul>
        <li><span class="hl k">Christian beliefs</span> — the nature of God (Trinity; omnipotent, loving, just), creation, incarnation, the last days and judgement.</li>
        <li><span class="hl g">Marriage and the family</span> — Christian views on marriage, sexual relationships, divorce, family and gender roles.</li>
        <li><span class="hl t">Matters of life and death</span> — sanctity of life, abortion, euthanasia, life after death, and responses to evolution and the Big Bang.</li>
        <li><span class="hl el">Ethical reasoning</span> — agape love, sanctity of life, situation ethics and the teachings of Jesus.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="note"><b>Spec focus:</b> you must <b>explain</b> Christian teachings, support them with <b>sources of authority</b> (the Bible, Church teaching), and evaluate them — noting that Christians do not always agree.</p>
    </section>

    <!-- 2 KEY TERMS -->
    <section class="screen" data-teach="key-terms">
      <span class="tag lo">Key vocabulary</span>
      <h2>Words you must be able to define</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><b>Agape</b> — selfless, unconditional love; the Christian love shown by Jesus (1 Corinthians 13).</li>
        <li><b>Sanctity of life</b> — the belief that life is <b>holy and God-given</b>, and so precious (Psalm 139).</li>
        <li><b>Incarnation</b> — the belief that God <b>became human in Jesus</b> ("the Word became flesh", John 1:14).</li>
        <li><b>Omnibenevolent</b> — <b>all-loving</b>; one of the qualities Christians give to God.</li>
        <li><b>Resurrection</b> — the belief that <b>Jesus rose from death</b> on the third day; the basis of Christian hope.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="note"><b>Why they matter:</b> these five ideas run through the whole topic. Sanctity of life shapes views on abortion and euthanasia; agape shapes situation ethics; the incarnation and resurrection are central Christian beliefs about who God is.</p>
    </section>

    <!-- 3 Q: define monotheism (MCQ) -->
    <section class="screen" data-test="q-mono">
      <span class="tag">Quick check</span>
      <h2>Define the term</h2>
      <div class="activity">
        <div class="qline"><span class="qnum">?</span><span>Which term means <b>the belief that life is holy and God-given</b>?</span></div>
        <div class="opts" data-q="q1" data-why="Sanctity of life = life is holy and belongs to God (Psalm 139). Agape is selfless love; incarnation is God becoming human in Jesus; resurrection is Jesus rising from death.">
          <button class="opt" data-correct="0">Agape <span class="mk">❌</span></button>
          <button class="opt" data-correct="1">Sanctity of life <span class="mk">✅</span></button>
          <button class="opt" data-correct="0">Incarnation <span class="mk">❌</span></button>
          <button class="opt" data-correct="0">Resurrection <span class="mk">❌</span></button>
        </div>
        <div class="feedback" id="fb-q1"></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 4 THE OMNI-ATTRIBUTES -->
    <section class="screen" data-teach="attributes">
      <span class="tag lo">Christian beliefs about God</span>
      <h2>The nature of God</h2>
      <p>Christians describe the one God using a set of key qualities. The specification highlights God as <b>omnipotent, loving (omnibenevolent) and just</b>, and as <b>Creator</b>:</p>
      <figure>
        <svg viewBox="0 0 560 250" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" role="img" aria-label="Christian beliefs about the nature of God: omnipotent, omnibenevolent, just, Creator and Trinity">
          <circle cx="280" cy="125" r="46" fill="#fff1c2" stroke="#2c2840" stroke-width="3"/>
          <text x="280" y="120" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Fredoka" font-size="15" font-weight="600" fill="#8b6a00">the one</text>
          <text x="280" y="140" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Fredoka" font-size="15" font-weight="600" fill="#8b6a00">God</text>
          <g font-family="Fredoka" font-weight="600" text-anchor="middle">
            <rect x="200" y="14" width="160" height="42" rx="12" fill="#d9ebff" stroke="#2c2840" stroke-width="2.5"/>
            <text x="280" y="33" font-size="13" fill="#0b5bbf">omnipotent</text>
            <text x="280" y="49" font-size="11" fill="#0b5bbf" font-weight="500">all-powerful</text>
            <line x1="280" y1="56" x2="280" y2="79" stroke="#2c2840" stroke-width="2"/>
            <rect x="18" y="70" width="160" height="42" rx="12" fill="#d6f6e4" stroke="#2c2840" stroke-width="2.5"/>
            <text x="98" y="89" font-size="13" fill="#137a45">omnibenevolent</text>
            <text x="98" y="105" font-size="11" fill="#137a45" font-weight="500">all-loving</text>
            <line x1="178" y1="95" x2="236" y2="115" stroke="#2c2840" stroke-width="2"/>
            <rect x="382" y="70" width="160" height="42" rx="12" fill="#ffdfe3" stroke="#2c2840" stroke-width="2.5"/>
            <text x="462" y="89" font-size="13" fill="#c8203a">just</text>
            <text x="462" y="105" font-size="11" fill="#c8203a" font-weight="500">fair judge</text>
            <line x1="382" y1="95" x2="324" y2="115" stroke="#2c2840" stroke-width="2"/>
            <rect x="18" y="150" width="160" height="42" rx="12" fill="#efe1ff" stroke="#2c2840" stroke-width="2.5"/>
            <text x="98" y="169" font-size="13" fill="#6a30b8">Trinity</text>
            <text x="98" y="185" font-size="11" fill="#6a30b8" font-weight="500">three persons</text>
            <line x1="178" y1="171" x2="236" y2="140" stroke="#2c2840" stroke-width="2"/>
            <rect x="382" y="150" width="160" height="42" rx="12" fill="#ffe9c7" stroke="#2c2840" stroke-width="2.5"/>
            <text x="462" y="169" font-size="13" fill="#9a5a00">Creator</text>
            <text x="462" y="185" font-size="11" fill="#9a5a00" font-weight="500">made all things</text>
            <line x1="382" y1="171" x2="324" y2="140" stroke="#2c2840" stroke-width="2"/>
          </g>
        </svg>
        <figcaption>Core Christian beliefs about God. God is <b>one</b>, yet exists as three persons — the <b>Trinity</b>.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <p class="note"><b>Why it matters:</b> because God is loving and all-powerful, Christians trust and pray to God; because God is just, they believe wrongdoing is answerable to God — so these beliefs shape worship, prayer and moral behaviour. A challenge Christians face is the <b>problem of evil</b>: how can a loving, all-powerful God allow suffering?</p>
    </section>

