    <!-- 6 CHRISTIANITY -->
    <section class="screen" data-teach="christianity">
      <span class="tag lo">Christian beliefs</span>
      <h2>One God in three persons</h2>
      <p>Christianity is <b>monotheistic</b>: there is one God. Christians also teach that this one God is a <span class="hl el">Trinity</span> — Father, Son (Jesus Christ) and Holy Spirit — as set out in the Creeds. The <b>incarnation</b> is the belief that the Son, God, became human in Jesus, and the <b>resurrection</b> (Jesus rising from death) is the foundation of Christian hope for life after death.</p>
      <figure>
        <svg viewBox="0 0 560 210" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" role="img" aria-label="Concept diagram of the Christian Trinity: one God, three persons">
          <text x="280" y="26" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Fredoka" font-size="15" font-weight="600" fill="#6a30b8">The Trinity — one God, three persons</text>
