    <!-- 21 HOW BELIEFS AFFECT BELIEVERS -->
    <section class="screen" data-teach="effects">
      <span class="tag lo">Why it matters</span>
      <h2>How beliefs shape Christian choices</h2>
      <p>Exam questions often ask how Christian <b>beliefs affect actions</b>. Christian ethics are not just ideas — they shape real decisions:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Believing God is <b>Creator</b> leads to <b>stewardship</b> — caring responsibly for the world.</li>
        <li>The <b>sanctity of life</b> shapes Christian views on abortion and euthanasia — protecting God-given life.</li>
        <li><b>Agape love</b> and the teachings of Jesus lead Christians to forgive, help the poor and welcome outsiders.</li>
        <li>Belief that marriage is a <b>lifelong covenant</b> shapes attitudes to divorce, faithfulness and family life.</li>
        <li>Belief in <b>judgement and life after death</b> encourages Christians to live morally now.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

